{
  "dom_id": "step-q11788",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Find the equation of the upward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point  $(8,12).$",
  "worked_solution": "We know that for any upward or downward-opening parabola whose vertex is $(0,0),$ the general standard equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe're told that the given parabola passes through the point $(8,12),$ so we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=12$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(12) \\\\ 64 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4py \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(\\frac{4}{3})y \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{16}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
